Subject: [PATCH 4/5] C13, patch 4 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M19; main's
 fourth folder, item 5): A GATE ON A VERDICT LINE THAT CLAIMS A SELECTION: ITS
 PAGE NAMES THE FAMILY OF ITS CRITERION

Main asks for a gate on a verdict line that claims a selection ("selects", "picks", "singles out", "forced"
with a value or a member as its object): it asks that the page name the family of the rule's third point, or
the arc is reported. With planted cases both ways.

THE GATE, selection-family, the 54th. It reads every verdict line from B1905 on. A clause of the line is a
claim when it says "selects", "picks", "singles out", "is forced" or "forces"; when no word of denial or of
condition stands before that word in its own clause; and when a value or a member is its object (a number,
an equation, a code, or a word that names one of several). A clause ends at a full stop, a semicolon, a
colon, a dash between spaces or a bracket, and an arc number in brackets is a citation and no value. The
page must name one of the two families: "finite classification" or "consistency condition". It is
registered with its failing-path test, and the practices page has its section.

WHY FROM B1905 ON, measured before it was written, as the card said it would be: over every older verdict
line, 115 read as claims by this reading, and the page of one of them names a family. Most are deductions
("m^2+4 = k^2 forces m = 0") that the rule is not about, and none was written under it. Held by name they
would be 114 names that say nothing. They are not read, and the gate prints their count, so that a change in
the reading shows. Main's choice, asked on the card: held by name, or read from the rule's arc on.

THE READING IS THE BUILDER'S AND MAIN'S TO CHANGE, and the test holds what it still does:
  - STILL PASSES: a claim with no value or member as its object ("the beat selects the spin structure"); a
    claim in other words than the five ("determines the value 3").
  - STILL REFUSED THOUGH HONEST: a deduction written with "forces" ("m^2+4 = k^2 forces m = 0"). From B1905
    on such a line names a family on its page or is reworded.

THE TESTS. tests/test_selection_family.py, five tests: six claims read and eight sentences that claim
nothing; a denial excuses only in its own clause and before the word, with its twin; what the reading still
passes and refuses; the family on the page, the line from which the gate reads, an older arc counted and not
read, a missing page; and the gate on this repository, with B1905's own line, which claims nothing, and its
page, which names both families. The failing-path test in tests/test_gate_failing_paths.py.

Every gate passes but the count of landings, and the stale-points check, which reads the day of the commit:
on this base, committed on 2026-11-13, six October rows are past 21 days. Main moved them on its head
(M22), and the series is built again there before it is sent.

Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it.

CORRECTED 2026-11-13, AFTER IT WAS FIRST SENT: this seat's own fault. As first sent, the gate's test named
real arcs as its planted ones (B1204, B1225, B287 and B1904 to B1907). The paper's verification package
counts every test file that names one of its records as a lock of that record, so its manifest went stale
and its test failed from this patch on. The planted arcs are now numbers that name no arc (B01204 and the
like). Nothing else of the patch is changed. Found while building card C14, by the paper's test.
